# Explicit reviewed plugin fixture

This wrapper composes the maintained Chimera shell and the licensed finite
`chimera-plugin-fixture` layer. Run the same explicit `npm ci`/typecheck/lint/build
and Go build commands in README; rendering performs no install/build/run.
The actual archive is carried in `third_party`, with raw SHA256/full MIT/source
notice, and the four byte-identical pinned adapters are recorded individually
in `plugin-provenance.json`. They are a source-distribution closure, not a public
frontend package. Formatting skips only those immutable vendor bytes; consumer
typecheck/build still verifies their actual imports.

One app-owned immutable generation g1 registry/bundle is served under root
`/plugins/registry` and `/plugins/recipe/g1/...`; it renders only in the declared
recipe.summary widget slot. React and Button are shared through the reviewed
Vite import map, never a parallel loader. Policy explicitly admits this reviewed
main-origin fixture; no sandbox/opaque-frame or untrusted plugin claim. Local
widget count/unload only affect transient presentation. The app APIs/health/chat
remain app-owned. There is no install/enable/business action/backend mutation.

The stylesheet lease removes only this fixture's generation-bound style on
unload or disposal. Use maintained APIs and a separately reviewed admission and
isolation policy for real plugins; do not replace the explicit review policy
with a silent main-origin fallback. Upgrades/publication remain separate work.
